{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.rho_trM_radial_handle_refuted_every_reading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.rho_trM_radial_handle_refuted_every_reading","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VolTHe3RadialHandle.lean#L88-L97","doc":"**Capstone.** `ρ = tr_M` radial handle is refuted under both available volume readings:\n(1) mass-braid closures degenerate (`Vol ≡ 0`, `degenerate_vol_kills_handle`); (2) binding-link volumes\nhyperbolic but unequal, and the true asymmetry keeps the prediction ratio on the opposite side of 1 from\n`C_knot` (`binding_link_vol_ratio_gt_one` ∧ `binding_link_pred_ratio_lt_one` ∧ `cknot_ratio_gt_one`).\nscope-(a); survivor is a derived `ρ ≠ tr_M`. Nothing wired; no fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.mirror_test_excludes_rho_trM_true_vol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.mirror_test_excludes_rho_trM_true_vol","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VolTHe3RadialHandle.lean#L69-L86","doc":"**Reading 2 — mirror test refuted with the TRUE (unequal) binding-link volumes.** Assume the radial\nansatz with the witnessed volumes and densities: `C_knot(T) = Vol(8₁₁)·tr_M(T)/h`,\n`C_knot(³He) = Vol(Borromean)·tr_M(³He)/h`. The general ratio identity forces\n`C_knot(T)/C_knot(³He) = (Vol(T)·tr_M(T))/(Vol(³He)·tr_M(³He))`, but the LHS is `> 1` and the RHS `< 1`\n— contradiction. Even the true volume asymmetry does not rescue `ρ = tr_M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.binding_link_vol_ratio_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.binding_link_vol_ratio_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VolTHe3RadialHandle.lean#L65-L67","doc":"**The binding-link volumes are genuinely unequal** (`Vol(T)/Vol(³He) > 1`). So \"mirror nuclei ⇒\nequal Vol\" is FALSE even for the hyperbolic binding-link reading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.binding_link_pred_ratio_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.binding_link_pred_ratio_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VolTHe3RadialHandle.lean#L59-L63","doc":"**The Vol·tr_M product ratio is below 1** at the TRUE binding-link volumes.\n`(Vol(8₁₁)·tr_M(T)) / (Vol(Borromean)·tr_M(³He)) = (8.2863168·0.104071)/(7.3277248·0.206578) ≈ 0.570`.\nThe volume asymmetry (8.2863168/7.3277248 ≈ 1.131, > 1) is far too weak to flip `tr_M`'s 0.504. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.cknot_ratio_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.cknot_ratio_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VolTHe3RadialHandle.lean#L56-L57","doc":"**C_knot mirror ratio exceeds 1** (T more bound). Master-formula μ_ext values (PR #4556). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.degenerate_vol_kills_handle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.degenerate_vol_kills_handle","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VolTHe3RadialHandle.lean#L47-L54","doc":"**A degenerate (zero) volume annihilates the handle.** If `Vol(K) = 0` then the radial dressing\n`Vol(K)·ρ(K)/h = 0`, so it cannot equal a nonzero `C_knot`. This is Reading 1: the mass-braid H₉\nclosures are non-hyperbolic (SnapPy), `Vol ≡ 0`, hence the handle is identically 0 and no nonzero\nbinding deficit is reproduced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.radial_ratio_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.VolTHe3RadialHandle.radial_ratio_general","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/VolTHe3RadialHandle.lean#L36-L45","doc":"**General two-volume ratio identity.** If `C_knot(K) = Vol(K)·ρ(K)/h` with a shared `h = ℏ_q²` but\npossibly DISTINCT volumes, then `C_knot(T)/C_knot(³He) = (Vol(T)·ρ(T))/(Vol(³He)·ρ(³He))` — only `h`\ncancels, the volume factor survives (generic field; `V_He, r_He, h ≠ 0`). Reduces to the equal-Vol\nidentity of `RadialVolRhoMirrorTest.mirror_ratio_of_radial` when `V_T = V_He`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}